  "c0x": "The cases were planned together along a gallery axis rather than one by one. Walnut base, slim-framed glass and hidden light repeat in every type, so the room reads as one system.",
  "i0t": "The gallery axis",
  "i0d": "Table, wall and plinth cases share one room; the common walnut body and glass language tie different sizes into one family.",
  "i1t": "In front of the wall case",
  "i1d": "A child and two adults look into the same case; shelf height and glass depth were set for different eye levels.",
  "i2t": "Table case at visitor scale",
  "i2d": "Visitors lean in to read the documents; the sloped fabric deck tilts photos and papers up towards the eye.",
  "c1t": "Wall cases",
  "c1x": "Objects read upright, such as documents, textiles and costume, sit in deep cases set against the wall. Light hides in the top profile and a linen back panel gives the object a calm ground.",
